{"id": "EUVD-2026-96589", "enisaUuid": "6f66c28b-989d-331d-8127-ebd94c6822b5", "description": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability in the getUserPermissionSet handler of SystemApiController that allows any authenticated user to read other users' permission codes. Low-privileged attackers can supply an arbitrary userId to GET /sys/api/getUserPermissionSet to retrieve the full permission set of any account, including administrators.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T21:49:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T16:01:15", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/JeecgBoot/poc_c096_sys_api_permission_set.py", "https://github.com/jeecgboot/JeecgBoot/blob/e3b9dc0aefe1943d9772b026f64ed671a7c82802/jeecg-boot/jeecg-module-system/jeecg-system-biz/src/main/java/org/jeecg/modules/api/controller/SystemApiController.java#L450-L453", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/jeecgboot-through-3.9.5-missing-authorization-via-sys-api-getuserpermissionset"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108650", "GHSA-2326-787x-9j94"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "945ea78f-d80e-3e57-8e87-af75812ffe73", "product": {"name": "JeecgBoot", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "bbe3e7c6-5efc-3b13-abf9-c739b87b1ca6", "vendor": {"name": "jeecgboot"}}], "isExploited": false}